=2 Walkthrough
!Beaucedine Glacier-map.jpg|right|Beaucedine Glacier
!Lower Delkfutt's Tower-map1.jpg|right|Lower Delkfutt First Floor
* **{c=red:Note:}** If you did not already do so, speak with {p:Cid} (in {p:Bastok} - {z:Metalworks} - Home Point #1) to begin this Mission.
* Head to (G-6) in {z:La Theine Plateau} and click on the **???** there. (The one where you talk to {p:Carbuncle}.)
** There are several other quests that begin at this **???** so you may need to watch several cutscenes to make sure you got the right one. It has Carbuncle and Tenzen in it.
** The {p:Unity Warp} (Level 99) will bring you close.

=4 Spiral
* Head to the Tower at (J-8) in {z:Beaucedine Glacier} and enter {z:Pso'Xja}.
** The {p:Unity Warp} (Level 125) will bring you close.
* This Tower is not a maze. There are a total of 16 **Stone Doors** that you must pass through normally, but each one of them has a high chance to spawn a {p:Gargoyle} when you check it.
** Defeat the {p:Gargoyle} and move through the Door quickly as it won't stay open for very long.
** Some things to remember:
*** The Doors cannot be opened from the other side (i.e. one-way). If you're in a party and someone doesn't make it through the Door in time, they will be stuck.
*** There are various other mobs in some of these rooms that are aggressive. Cryptonberries aggro to {@a:Sight|Detects by Sight} Sight, {m:Magic Millstones|Magic Millstone} aggro {@a:Magic|Detects by Magic} Magic.
*** These monsters WILL aggro you through the Doors so take caution fighting close to the next Door.
*** It is possible for a {p:Thief} to pick the trap and open the Door without spawning a {p:Gargoyle}, although it rarely works.
*** Some Doors may not spawn anything and simply open. (15/16 doors spawned Gargoyle for me)
* After you have made your way past all 16 Doors, sneak up and head down the elevator.
* Check the **Avatar Gate** at the bottom for a cutscene.

=4 Branded
* Head to (G-10) in {z:Upper Jeuno} - Home Point #3 and speak with {n:Monberaux} for a cutscene to obtain a {@k} {k:Envelope from Monberaux}.
* Speak with {n:Pherimociel} at (G-6) - Home Point #1 - in {z:Ru'Lude Gardens} for a cutscene.
* Return to {n:Monberaux} in {z:Upper Jeuno} for some dialogue.

=4 Pride and Honor
* Enter {z:Batallia Downs} from {z:Upper Jeuno}. Next to the other side of the wall near the entrance to town, near Acacia at (K-8/9), there is a **???**. Check it for a cutscene.
* Check the ??? again to obtain a {@k} {k:Delkfutt recognition device}.
* Head to the entrance of {z:Lower Delkfutt's Tower}.
** The fastest way if you have at least {k:White stratum abyssite III} from {p:Voidwatch|Voidwatch Quests} is the {p:Atmacite Refiner} you're already standing next to:
*** Request teleportation. > Jeuno. > Delkfutt's Tower (entrance).
** The {p:Survival Guide} just inside the tower is fastest otherwise
* Go to (H-5) on the first floor of {z:Lower Delkfutt's Tower} and check the **Cermet Door** to spawn a {m:Disaster Idol}.
** This mob uses normal {m:Doll} moves, as well as casting Tier 3-ga spells and Tier 4 single target spells based on the current Vana'diel day.
** If in a party, the {m:Disaster Idol} only needs to be killed once
* After you defeat the {m:Disaster Idol}, check the **Cermet Door** once again for a cutscene.

=4 And the Compass Guides
!PsoXja 60 Cap Directions.jpg|right|Pso'Xja Guide
* Head to the tower at (H-10) in {z:Beaucedine Glacier} and enter {z:Pso'Xja} for a cutscene.
** Enemies in this tower will aggro level 99 players. Make sure you have some {@i:Silent Oil|4165} {i:Silent Oils|Silent Oil|4165} and {@i:Prism Powder|4164} {i:Prism Powders|Prism Powder|4164}.
** The {p:Unity Warp} (Level 125) will bring you close.
* There are a few one way walls in here that can be confusing. Walk around the outer perimeter of the map until you are almost back where you started (I-8).
* Head west through the wall and drop through a hole in the floor.
* Exit the room to the south, follow the hallway, and enter the room to the north at the end of the hallway.
* Take the elevator down to the **Avatar Gate** for a cutscene.
* Return to {p:Cid} once again to finish this path.

----
* If you have completed the other 2 paths ({M:Ulmia's Path|Promathia Mission 5-3/Ulmia's Path|Where Messengers Gather}, {M:Louverance's Path|Promathia Mission 5-3/Louverance's Path|Past Sins}), {p:Cid} will give an additional cutscene and you can move on to the next Chapter: **{M:For Whom the Verse is Sung|Promathia Mission 6-1|For Whom the Verse is Sung}**.

